1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,800
Why is it so important for me to be an idol?

2
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:05,500
Welcome to the Zombieland Saga Project, baby!

3
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,000
We're gonna do the local idol thing?

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:08,000
We need a new name!

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
What do I do?

6
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,000
It's perfect fun!

7
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Don't freak out. I'll be there to back you.

8
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,500
Whether or not you have what it takes is irrelevant because I do!

9
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,500
Can we go back to the way things were?

10
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,000
It was a crazy idea in the first place.

11
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,500
This project has a crucial deadline.

12
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,000
No doubt about it. All those girls are dead.

13
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:28,500
Hey, maybe he raised them from the dead like a bunch of zombies.

14
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Uh...

15
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Why am I smiling right now?

16
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:48,000
We can say, oh my God, that's neck and Eig gibi UP.

17
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:59,000
I'm young.

18
00:02:00,028 --> 00:02:30,008
To be continued...

19
00:02:30,028 --> 00:02:33,588
I betcha we can bring in a thousand people for the next show!

20
00:02:33,748 --> 00:02:36,348
If we start getting cocky, then we're sure to make a mistake.

21
00:02:36,508 --> 00:02:37,468
We should focus.

22
00:02:38,008 --> 00:02:39,348
Work calmly and steadily.

23
00:02:39,808 --> 00:02:40,148
Cool!

24
00:02:40,448 --> 00:02:43,088
So I say we do that nerdy crap Junko just said,

25
00:02:43,448 --> 00:02:44,768
and bring in that thousand!

26
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:45,688
Yeah!

27
00:02:48,068 --> 00:02:49,728
If the movies have taught me anything,

28
00:02:49,848 --> 00:02:53,248
it's that zombies with big fat heads are way easier to kill!

29
00:02:54,668 --> 00:02:57,948
Look, if you brain-rotted suckers keep on riding the high from Arpino,

30
00:02:58,148 --> 00:02:58,948
then it's BOOM!

31
00:02:59,148 --> 00:02:59,668
Headshot!

32
00:03:00,028 --> 00:03:03,008
Next show will be at Ekimai Furosan Stadium!

33
00:03:03,428 --> 00:03:04,868
EFS if you're nasty!

34
00:03:06,408 --> 00:03:07,748
Wait, I'm confused.

35
00:03:08,108 --> 00:03:09,008
Where'd you say again?

36
00:03:09,848 --> 00:03:10,608
What's wrong?

37
00:03:11,008 --> 00:03:13,688
Yeah, I don't think I've ever heard of that venue before.

38
00:03:14,108 --> 00:03:16,388
Eh, not like I care where they call the place.

39
00:03:16,588 --> 00:03:19,508
Point is, we're putting a thousand butts in the seats this time.

40
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:20,388
Actually,

41
00:03:21,248 --> 00:03:23,428
the name won't be changed until February.

42
00:03:24,028 --> 00:03:26,028
I see somebody's done their homework.

43
00:03:26,028 --> 00:03:28,048
Oh, no wonder it doesn't ring a bell.

44
00:03:28,788 --> 00:03:29,988
So what's it called now?

45
00:03:29,988 --> 00:03:32,828
The best amenity stadium.

46
00:03:32,828 --> 00:03:35,628
The huge one in Tosu.

47
00:03:35,628 --> 00:03:40,468
Uh, isn't that...

48
00:03:40,468 --> 00:03:42,248
I promise I'll be okay.

49
00:03:42,248 --> 00:03:45,188
The biggest issue is the size of the place.

50
00:03:45,188 --> 00:03:48,588
I think the capacity is around...

51
00:03:48,588 --> 00:03:49,588
25,000.

52
00:03:49,588 --> 00:03:50,248
25,000?

53
00:03:50,248 --> 00:03:51,428
That's like 50 Arpinos!

54
00:03:51,428 --> 00:03:58,008
And with the field, there's standing room for even more.

55
00:03:58,728 --> 00:04:02,028
If this thing goes south, could I take out that many people?

56
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:03,628
This is a really big deal.

57
00:04:03,628 --> 00:04:05,128
There's no way we'll pull it off!

58
00:04:05,128 --> 00:04:09,088
The concert is scheduled for March 8th.

59
00:04:09,088 --> 00:04:09,948
Don't be an idiot!

60
00:04:10,488 --> 00:04:12,448
A whole stadium here in Saga?

61
00:04:12,828 --> 00:04:14,168
We could never fill it up!

62
00:04:14,648 --> 00:04:15,928
Iron Frill did it back then, but...

63
00:04:15,928 --> 00:04:18,448
So that was them then, and this is you now!

64
00:04:20,448 --> 00:04:21,628
Oh, I'm sorry.

65
00:04:22,028 --> 00:04:25,928
Do you knuckleheads honestly believe Iron Frill was better 10 years ago than you are today?

66
00:04:25,988 --> 00:04:27,248
Because that is idiotic!

67
00:04:28,248 --> 00:04:31,268
Your legends, each and every...

68
00:04:31,268 --> 00:04:37,328
All except one of you, that is.

69
00:04:37,748 --> 00:04:39,268
Don't single me out or anything.

70
00:04:39,728 --> 00:04:43,408
I hand-selected you girls to come back to life and bring Saga to life, too!

71
00:04:43,628 --> 00:04:44,708
You can accomplish anything!

72
00:04:44,708 --> 00:04:48,668
So on March 8th, EFS will be jam-packed with your fans!

73
00:04:49,188 --> 00:04:52,688
I say, get the crowd all fired up and encore with that new number!

74
00:04:53,048 --> 00:04:53,448
Yeah!

75
00:04:56,328 --> 00:04:58,188
This bomb is still lit!

76
00:04:58,488 --> 00:05:00,668
Soon everyone will know Frans Choushu!

77
00:05:03,768 --> 00:05:08,768
Shades is always drinking the dumbass juice, but even I can tell he chugged the whole bottle this time.

78
00:05:09,028 --> 00:05:10,208
Is this really gonna work?

79
00:05:10,388 --> 00:05:12,168
Normally, I'd say it's impossible.

80
00:05:12,588 --> 00:05:14,208
You're right, it's just not realistic.

81
00:05:14,208 --> 00:05:15,168
Yeah, but...

82
00:05:15,168 --> 00:05:15,768
Yeah, but...

83
00:05:15,768 --> 00:05:16,388
I know.

84
00:05:16,668 --> 00:05:18,788
We're long past considering what's realistic.

85
00:05:19,428 --> 00:05:20,188
Good point.

86
00:05:20,468 --> 00:05:26,228
If Mr. Kotaro's really this dead set on it, maybe he's got a good reason we don't know about yet.

87
00:05:26,448 --> 00:05:28,248
Doesn't he just pull stuff out of his butt?

88
00:05:28,248 --> 00:05:34,588
I say... we try.

89
00:05:34,588 --> 00:05:35,388
Huh?

90
00:05:35,388 --> 00:05:37,928
Do you realize what a big risk this is?

91
00:05:37,928 --> 00:05:39,488
I don't know if we'll be successful.

92
00:05:39,488 --> 00:05:44,368
But if it's a chance for all of us to sing and dance together, then I'm more than up for it.

93
00:05:44,368 --> 00:05:47,748
What matters to me is performing with you guys.

94
00:05:47,748 --> 00:05:50,048
You're on.

95
00:05:50,048 --> 00:05:52,508
You're right, the show Arpino is terrible.

96
00:05:52,508 --> 00:05:54,068
And we made it through that.

97
00:05:54,068 --> 00:05:57,028
Besides, everything that we do is bold and brazen.

98
00:05:57,028 --> 00:05:59,228
Yeah, I mean, we're already zombies.

99
00:05:59,968 --> 00:06:02,348
So it's not like this is gonna kill us, am I right?

100
00:06:02,408 --> 00:06:06,768
Just listening to each of you talk makes me feel like we can actually do this.

101
00:06:07,088 --> 00:06:08,108
I'm kind of shocked.

102
00:06:08,108 --> 00:06:13,128
What am I gonna do with you crazies?

103
00:06:13,868 --> 00:06:17,568
For this to work out, we need the show to be even better than Arpino.

104
00:06:17,568 --> 00:06:20,748
If we do anything less than our best, then we're certain to fail.

105
00:06:21,048 --> 00:06:23,108
Okay, now whip us into shape, I.

106
00:06:23,468 --> 00:06:24,348
No problem.

107
00:06:24,628 --> 00:06:27,388
Time to address everything I've been letting you guys slide on.

108
00:06:27,528 --> 00:06:27,868
Mm-hmm.

109
00:06:28,288 --> 00:06:29,188
Mostly you.

110
00:06:29,368 --> 00:06:31,548
Uh, come on, don't be too mean.

111
00:06:31,848 --> 00:06:32,408
What's wrong?

112
00:06:32,488 --> 00:06:33,368
You can't handle it.

113
00:06:34,428 --> 00:06:34,608
Ha!

114
00:06:38,108 --> 00:06:44,668
Looks like there's still something bugging you.

115
00:06:45,048 --> 00:06:46,648
Well, how could this not bug me?

116
00:06:47,268 --> 00:06:49,008
It is where I died, after all.

117
00:06:49,348 --> 00:06:50,548
You can't die twice.

118
00:06:50,728 --> 00:06:51,988
No point in being scared.

119
00:06:51,988 --> 00:06:55,688
I don't think you're the one to talk to since you jumped off the same cliff twice.

120
00:06:59,408 --> 00:07:00,128
Hey, Ai.

121
00:07:00,588 --> 00:07:02,428
Remember what you said back at the park?

122
00:07:02,928 --> 00:07:04,628
I don't care if I'm a zombie.

123
00:07:05,048 --> 00:07:06,928
I'm gonna get back on stage again.

124
00:07:06,928 --> 00:07:08,708
And then I'll...

125
00:07:08,708 --> 00:07:10,108
Let's make it happen.

126
00:07:10,608 --> 00:07:12,968
If something goes wrong, I'll take care of it for us.

127
00:07:13,428 --> 00:07:16,228
I'm the boss, and the boss can't be afraid to get her hands dirty.

128
00:07:16,788 --> 00:07:17,948
Leader, not boss.

129
00:07:18,088 --> 00:07:18,868
Same thing.

130
00:07:19,648 --> 00:07:20,088
Huh?

131
00:07:20,608 --> 00:07:21,748
Damn, that's scary!

132
00:07:22,168 --> 00:07:24,348
I wanted to make sure you guys were okay.

133
00:07:24,888 --> 00:07:25,708
Um, yeah.

134
00:07:25,968 --> 00:07:27,588
It wasn't anything serious, sir.

135
00:07:27,588 --> 00:07:28,248
We'll be fine.

136
00:07:28,248 --> 00:07:30,548
I'll be there to back you up, too.

137
00:07:31,308 --> 00:07:33,868
And I'm sorry for eavesdropping, but I couldn't help it.

138
00:07:34,268 --> 00:07:34,768
I know!

139
00:07:34,968 --> 00:07:36,848
We should have a rally to build up our morale!

140
00:07:37,408 --> 00:07:39,268
We're idols, not bikers, Saki.

141
00:07:39,268 --> 00:07:50,848
No, that isn't it.

142
00:07:52,428 --> 00:07:54,168
There's no way we'll pull it off!

143
00:07:57,668 --> 00:07:59,368
La, la, la, loo, la, loo, la...

144
00:07:59,368 --> 00:08:00,328
That doesn't work.

145
00:08:04,048 --> 00:08:05,928
This place is huge.

146
00:08:05,928 --> 00:08:07,768
Question.

147
00:08:08,168 --> 00:08:08,408
Hmm.

148
00:08:08,688 --> 00:08:11,748
I was too nervous to ask before, but...

149
00:08:11,748 --> 00:08:14,548
Would you mind telling me how many tickets we've sold so far?

150
00:08:14,828 --> 00:08:15,848
I didn't print any.

151
00:08:16,348 --> 00:08:16,788
Huh?

152
00:08:17,268 --> 00:08:18,308
What did you say?

153
00:08:18,528 --> 00:08:20,108
We're only selling them day of.

154
00:08:20,548 --> 00:08:22,168
But why would you do that?

155
00:08:22,268 --> 00:08:26,628
With this concert, we need to put out the message that Franshushu has risen in Saga.

156
00:08:27,088 --> 00:08:30,428
That means it should be legendary in as many ways as possible.

157
00:08:30,948 --> 00:08:32,468
Ordinary methods won't cut it.

158
00:08:32,468 --> 00:08:36,228
Remember everything you've accomplished so far.

159
00:08:37,228 --> 00:08:40,628
Believe in Franshushu, and believe in me as well.

160
00:08:50,208 --> 00:08:51,668
Oh my gosh.

161
00:08:51,808 --> 00:08:54,168
The whole crowd fits in the VIP area.

162
00:08:54,168 --> 00:08:56,728
Um, hey guys.

163
00:08:57,188 --> 00:08:57,948
Glad you're here.

164
00:08:58,448 --> 00:09:02,228
We are, uh, Franshushu.

165
00:09:02,228 --> 00:09:02,448
Come on.

166
00:09:23,528 --> 00:09:24,528
Oh my gosh.

167
00:09:24,528 --> 00:09:34,908
Should we yell for an encore?

168
00:09:35,328 --> 00:09:36,208
No way, Chul.

169
00:09:36,828 --> 00:09:37,708
Better be cruel.

170
00:09:38,928 --> 00:09:40,548
Could this be the end?

171
00:09:54,528 --> 00:10:12,508
Ladies, I'm home!

172
00:10:12,508 --> 00:10:17,328
Oh look, if it isn't the legendary Fryster Pooh!

173
00:10:17,468 --> 00:10:19,008
Mr. Kotaro, where were you?

174
00:10:19,188 --> 00:10:20,248
We've been worried sick!

175
00:10:20,268 --> 00:10:21,768
Don't you worry, baby Zed.

176
00:10:21,768 --> 00:10:24,848
You know, your trusty old commander won't go MIA forever?

177
00:10:27,668 --> 00:10:29,528
Don't tell me you were drinking all night.

178
00:10:29,648 --> 00:10:30,448
Yeah, obviously.

179
00:10:30,828 --> 00:10:31,788
Because guess what, girls?

180
00:10:31,868 --> 00:10:35,368
We are drowning in debt now for about 20 mil.

181
00:10:36,648 --> 00:10:37,708
Crazy, ain't it?

182
00:10:37,808 --> 00:10:38,728
Yes, sirree.

183
00:10:38,908 --> 00:10:40,968
We are 20 million dee.

184
00:10:41,168 --> 00:10:41,928
We're in debt?

185
00:10:42,588 --> 00:10:43,888
No, that can't be right.

186
00:10:44,128 --> 00:10:44,728
No way.

187
00:10:45,268 --> 00:10:46,228
I mean, yeah.

188
00:10:46,548 --> 00:10:49,708
That was a large-scale concert and it failed tremendously.

189
00:10:49,708 --> 00:10:51,288
Of course we're in debt.

190
00:10:51,768 --> 00:10:52,888
Relax!

191
00:10:53,428 --> 00:10:54,888
No use of crying now!

192
00:10:55,028 --> 00:10:56,228
Front Shoo Shoo's done for!

193
00:10:56,428 --> 00:10:57,768
Saga's done for too!

194
00:10:57,908 --> 00:10:59,008
It's all done!

195
00:10:59,248 --> 00:11:00,888
Let's pack it in, everybody!

196
00:11:02,828 --> 00:11:06,028
Shades has been on his little bender for two whole weeks now.

197
00:11:06,708 --> 00:11:09,348
And our food supply's been depleted for seven days.

198
00:11:09,928 --> 00:11:13,068
Yeah, but zombies don't need to eat, so it's not that big of an issue, right?

199
00:11:13,388 --> 00:11:14,048
Who knows?

200
00:11:14,128 --> 00:11:17,048
Maybe he's coming up with an amazing plan to fix all this right now.

201
00:11:17,208 --> 00:11:18,388
He's done it before, remember?

202
00:11:19,028 --> 00:11:21,008
That asshat doesn't plan for crap!

203
00:11:21,208 --> 00:11:23,088
That's how we ended up in this whole mess!

204
00:11:23,448 --> 00:11:25,368
Hey, don't take your feelings out on Sakura.

205
00:11:25,628 --> 00:11:27,708
You're not the only one who's irritated, you know.

206
00:11:28,028 --> 00:11:29,348
Then I'll take him out on you!

207
00:11:29,728 --> 00:11:30,968
Please don't fight, you two.

208
00:11:31,108 --> 00:11:33,108
It's times like this we need to stick together.

209
00:11:33,368 --> 00:11:36,068
We'll be okay somehow, even if he gives up on us.

210
00:11:36,068 --> 00:11:40,048
You say that, but without Mr. Tatsumi's help, we can't do our makeup.

211
00:11:40,308 --> 00:11:42,428
Which means we can't go shopping or anything either.

212
00:11:42,928 --> 00:11:45,688
And the longer this goes on, the bigger our debt is going to get.

213
00:11:46,068 --> 00:11:50,648
I'm sorry, Sakura, but it'll take a lot more than positivity to take care of this problem.

214
00:11:57,308 --> 00:11:57,788
Tai?

215
00:11:58,688 --> 00:12:00,628
Damn, your face looks busted.

216
00:12:06,068 --> 00:12:17,268
She got that by herself?

217
00:12:17,528 --> 00:12:18,628
I guess.

218
00:12:18,788 --> 00:12:20,368
Which means she swiped his cash?

219
00:12:20,448 --> 00:12:21,748
And painted her face?

220
00:12:21,768 --> 00:12:22,008
Mm-hmm.

221
00:12:22,988 --> 00:12:24,168
That's crazy.

222
00:12:27,748 --> 00:12:28,968
This proves it.

223
00:12:29,208 --> 00:12:30,208
We were wrong.

224
00:12:31,028 --> 00:12:34,168
We can do anything if we try, just like Tai did.

225
00:12:34,168 --> 00:12:37,368
The problem is, we haven't been trying our best.

226
00:12:37,808 --> 00:12:40,048
We're so used to him calling the shots.

227
00:12:40,788 --> 00:12:43,348
And with him gone, we assumed that we had to give up.

228
00:12:43,468 --> 00:12:43,768
Yeah.

229
00:12:44,288 --> 00:12:47,568
At some point, we started relying on him too much and took him for granted.

230
00:12:48,008 --> 00:12:48,408
Right.

231
00:12:48,628 --> 00:12:50,468
That's what happened with the EFS show.

232
00:12:50,988 --> 00:12:54,928
All we thought was that if we do our best, he'll make everything else come together.

233
00:12:55,868 --> 00:12:57,408
And clearly, that's not true.

234
00:12:59,408 --> 00:13:02,308
Since we've got the makeup, guess we might as well use it.

235
00:13:02,308 --> 00:13:04,608
Sounds fun, but how do we pay out the debt?

236
00:13:04,988 --> 00:13:05,688
By working.

237
00:13:05,888 --> 00:13:10,248
If we can't do idle stuff right now, then let's try to get part-time jobs until it's possible.

238
00:13:10,648 --> 00:13:11,028
Cool.

239
00:13:11,148 --> 00:13:12,228
Can I help out too?

240
00:13:12,608 --> 00:13:13,088
Sure.

241
00:13:13,308 --> 00:13:14,108
Let's do it.

242
00:13:14,348 --> 00:13:14,668
Yeah.

243
00:13:14,848 --> 00:13:15,988
We're good under pressure.

244
00:13:16,648 --> 00:13:18,568
Time for us to do the thinking ourselves.

245
00:13:18,788 --> 00:13:21,768
We can move forward without letting the past bring us down.

246
00:13:21,768 --> 00:13:27,208
That's right.

247
00:13:27,488 --> 00:13:29,208
In the end, I still happened.

248
00:13:30,828 --> 00:13:31,648
What's up?

249
00:13:32,548 --> 00:13:33,288
I'm in.

250
00:13:34,068 --> 00:13:36,888
We may be zombies, but there's still life in us.

251
00:13:37,308 --> 00:13:38,188
You're right.

252
00:13:38,548 --> 00:13:40,968
Let's work hard so we can get our revenge.

253
00:13:40,968 --> 00:13:56,468
That's a shame.

254
00:13:56,788 --> 00:13:57,688
He's dead as dirt.

255
00:13:58,188 --> 00:13:59,088
What's all that?

256
00:13:59,288 --> 00:14:00,428
Just a bunch of squid?

257
00:14:00,688 --> 00:14:01,428
Looks that way.

258
00:14:01,688 --> 00:14:02,868
I'm not sure why, though.

259
00:14:03,048 --> 00:14:04,048
He coughed!

260
00:14:04,108 --> 00:14:05,148
Oh, he's alive!

261
00:14:05,148 --> 00:14:05,908
You all right?

262
00:14:05,908 --> 00:14:10,928
I'm better than ever.

263
00:14:11,228 --> 00:14:12,988
Just got a little swept away is all.

264
00:14:18,028 --> 00:14:19,868
And then the guy walked off!

265
00:14:20,028 --> 00:14:21,628
Dude, how crazy is that?

266
00:14:21,788 --> 00:14:23,868
We got ourselves a mysterious squid man.

267
00:14:24,428 --> 00:14:25,888
I'll let you take that one.

268
00:14:26,088 --> 00:14:26,348
What?

269
00:14:26,968 --> 00:14:29,088
Well, your story must be pretty important, then.

270
00:14:29,608 --> 00:14:32,528
I think even the Tokyo pubs are going to want this.

271
00:14:32,808 --> 00:14:33,368
Oh, really?

272
00:14:33,628 --> 00:14:34,188
Clock's ticking.

273
00:14:34,488 --> 00:14:34,768
Right.

274
00:14:34,988 --> 00:14:35,288
Gotcha.

275
00:14:35,908 --> 00:14:38,688
Later, then, I got myself a squid man to track down.

276
00:14:46,488 --> 00:14:47,368
Morning, ladies.

277
00:14:47,748 --> 00:14:49,068
What happened to you?

278
00:14:49,388 --> 00:14:49,868
Irrelevant.

279
00:14:54,488 --> 00:14:55,288
Aren't you gonna—

280
00:14:55,288 --> 00:14:58,308
One year ago, I made a big mistake.

281
00:14:58,308 --> 00:15:04,028
On the last 8th of March, at my behest, you performed in a show that failed enormously.

282
00:15:04,028 --> 00:15:05,028
I'm sorry.

283
00:15:05,028 --> 00:15:05,508
I'm sorry.

284
00:15:08,648 --> 00:15:11,688
That's why next month, you will return to EFS.

285
00:15:11,688 --> 00:15:13,988
Your revenge show is March 8th.

286
00:15:17,988 --> 00:15:19,988
Your revenge show is March 8th.

287
00:15:19,988 --> 00:15:20,348
Hey!

288
00:15:20,348 --> 00:15:22,968
That said, the approach will be different.

289
00:15:22,968 --> 00:15:24,968
I'm not just banking on our momentum.

290
00:15:24,968 --> 00:15:29,508
This year, you've breathed new life into Franz Shushu.

291
00:15:29,508 --> 00:15:36,128
Your album and merch sales have been plentiful, like the rice in the fields of Hanamura and Warabino.

292
00:15:36,128 --> 00:15:40,028
More importantly, the seven of you have truly grown.

293
00:15:40,028 --> 00:15:44,188
But despite all that, this show won't be easy.

294
00:15:44,188 --> 00:15:48,868
Right now, I'm working on a variety of advertising projects to build up some hype.

295
00:15:48,868 --> 00:15:52,288
I promise you girls, I'm giving this all I have.

296
00:15:52,288 --> 00:15:59,288
Someday, when Franz Shushu is an even greater known legend, that failure will be a brief chapter in our tale.

297
00:15:59,288 --> 00:16:02,288
That's why you picked March 8th.

298
00:16:02,288 --> 00:16:03,288
Listen!

299
00:16:03,288 --> 00:16:05,288
This battle will be fierce.

300
00:16:05,288 --> 00:16:06,288
But take heart!

301
00:16:06,288 --> 00:16:10,288
Because of your heroic act, Saga will be forever changed!

302
00:16:10,288 --> 00:16:16,288
Even if Saga itself is plunged into darkness and despair, the seven of you will still remain!

303
00:16:16,288 --> 00:16:22,288
A bright light, shining eternally throughout that pit of oblivion!

304
00:16:22,288 --> 00:16:23,288
Never forget!

305
00:16:23,288 --> 00:16:28,288
I hand-selected each of you to come back from the dead to become the new heroes of Saga!

306
00:16:28,288 --> 00:16:37,288
And when your revenge is set into motion, that's the signal for Saga's counterattack to begin!

307
00:16:40,288 --> 00:16:41,288
What's with the sneeze?

308
00:16:41,288 --> 00:16:42,288
A little cold.

309
00:16:42,288 --> 00:16:43,288
I thought it was cute.

310
00:16:43,288 --> 00:16:45,288
That killed the whole thing!

311
00:16:45,288 --> 00:16:46,288
Oh!

312
00:16:46,288 --> 00:16:47,288
Shut up!

313
00:16:54,288 --> 00:16:56,288
Kotaro Tatsumi, isn't it?

314
00:16:58,288 --> 00:17:00,288
I'm Arata Okuba.

315
00:17:00,288 --> 00:17:02,288
I write for Saga Zine.

316
00:17:02,288 --> 00:17:03,288
Yeah.

317
00:17:03,288 --> 00:17:05,288
I read your articles pretty often.

318
00:17:05,288 --> 00:17:08,288
It's a shame what happened a year ago.

319
00:17:08,288 --> 00:17:12,288
But it seems like your girls have been really outdoing themselves recently.

320
00:17:12,288 --> 00:17:15,288
Are you here to reflect on past mistakes?

321
00:17:15,288 --> 00:17:16,288
Sorry.

322
00:17:16,288 --> 00:17:18,288
I'm not doing personal interviews.

323
00:17:18,288 --> 00:17:22,288
You stay in my line of work long enough and you end up with acquaintances all over the place.

324
00:17:23,288 --> 00:17:26,288
That said, it took me a while to connect the dots this time.

325
00:17:26,288 --> 00:17:37,288
Sakura Minamoto, Saki Nikaido, Ai Mizuno, Miss Junko Kono, Lily Hoshikawa slash Masao Go, and Tai Yamada.

326
00:17:37,288 --> 00:17:40,288
All of those people are dead.

327
00:17:40,288 --> 00:17:45,288
Sadly, I wasn't able to dig up any until about number five.

328
00:17:45,288 --> 00:17:46,288
Heh.

329
00:17:46,288 --> 00:17:48,288
You ready to talk?

330
00:17:48,288 --> 00:17:50,288
What exactly are these women?

331
00:17:51,288 --> 00:17:53,288
These pictures beg a lot of questions.

332
00:17:55,288 --> 00:17:57,288
I can have their graves exhumed, you know.

333
00:17:58,288 --> 00:18:00,288
Why write something like this?

334
00:18:00,288 --> 00:18:07,288
Because I feel compelled to stop you from trying to profit off these poor deceased girls by turning them into singing and dancing clowns.

335
00:18:07,288 --> 00:18:09,288
Is that reason enough for you?

336
00:18:09,288 --> 00:18:12,288
Feel free to stay silent.

337
00:18:12,288 --> 00:18:15,288
But after the article is published, your big secret will be out.

338
00:18:16,288 --> 00:18:17,288
It's shocking news.

339
00:18:18,288 --> 00:18:19,288
I wonder what the public will think.

340
00:18:21,288 --> 00:18:24,288
They'll be here next month, performing in a big concert.

341
00:18:25,288 --> 00:18:26,288
What?

342
00:18:26,288 --> 00:18:27,288
It's their revenge.

343
00:18:27,288 --> 00:18:28,288
You're insane.

344
00:18:28,288 --> 00:18:30,288
Why would you want to recreate such a disaster?

345
00:18:30,288 --> 00:18:33,288
How dare you turn the dead into cheap entertainment?

346
00:18:34,288 --> 00:18:38,288
You can publish anything you like, but you'll never stop Franshu Shuu.

347
00:18:39,288 --> 00:18:44,288
I'll make sure they don't take that stage.

348
00:18:55,288 --> 00:18:56,288
You okay down there?

349
00:19:01,288 --> 00:19:05,288
The high school girl kept her mouth shut, but I doubt it'll work out that way this time.

350
00:19:05,288 --> 00:19:09,288
Though if I'm being honest, I was a little surprised that the word didn't get out sooner.

351
00:19:10,288 --> 00:19:12,288
And the reporter's not your only problem.

352
00:19:13,288 --> 00:19:17,288
Things have been rough lately, but this'll be worse than some scratches and stolen clothes.

353
00:19:18,288 --> 00:19:19,288
I don't care about that crap.

354
00:19:20,288 --> 00:19:22,288
This show is gonna be a roaring success.

355
00:19:23,288 --> 00:19:24,288
I won't screw up again.

356
00:19:25,288 --> 00:19:31,288
Hm. Twelve years ago, when I first ran into that gloomy half-crazed kid, I never thought he could make all of this happen.

357
00:19:31,288 --> 00:19:36,288
If I wasn't gloomy and half-crazed, then I doubt I would have believed you.

358
00:19:37,288 --> 00:19:41,288
That you're immortal, fighting a curse that's been at work in Saga for centuries.

359
00:19:42,288 --> 00:19:44,288
And that part about how you can revive the dead.

360
00:19:44,288 --> 00:19:46,288
Hm. But you got what you wanted.

361
00:19:47,288 --> 00:19:48,288
Not yet.

362
00:19:49,288 --> 00:19:52,288
I still have to find a way to stop your prophecy from coming true.

363
00:19:53,288 --> 00:19:57,288
As the Rewa era starts, Saga will face a cataclysmic threat.

364
00:19:58,288 --> 00:20:01,288
A powerful phenomenon will cause thoughts of Saga to disappear,

365
00:20:01,288 --> 00:20:04,288
and even memories of Saga's past will be lost forever.

366
00:20:05,288 --> 00:20:08,288
Of course, things were already looking dire enough with the population decreasing.

367
00:20:09,288 --> 00:20:13,288
Exactly. So the obvious solution was to create something in Saga that's impossible to forget.

368
00:20:13,288 --> 00:20:18,288
Gathering young women killed by the curse who otherwise would have brought glory to this region,

369
00:20:19,288 --> 00:20:22,288
and making them into a popular idol group that the people of Saga can be proud of?

370
00:20:23,288 --> 00:20:27,288
I admit, it's a great idea, this Mount Mifuneyama Rakuin project of yours.

371
00:20:28,288 --> 00:20:30,288
It's called the Zombieland Saga Project.

372
00:20:31,288 --> 00:20:32,288
That's what I meant.

373
00:20:33,288 --> 00:20:36,288
The world is shaped by the actions of men.

374
00:20:36,288 --> 00:20:38,288
You're wrong there.

375
00:20:39,288 --> 00:20:40,288
Men and zombies.

376
00:20:41,288 --> 00:20:43,288
It's both, hand in hand.

377
00:20:47,288 --> 00:20:51,288
All of Kyushu is under a severe rain warning tonight and into tomorrow morning.

378
00:20:54,288 --> 00:20:55,288
That's a lot of rain.

379
00:20:56,288 --> 00:20:57,288
I wonder if Kokoro's okay?

380
00:20:58,288 --> 00:20:59,288
He'll be fine.

381
00:21:00,288 --> 00:21:01,288
I sure hope so.

382
00:21:01,288 --> 00:21:03,288
When he gets back, we ought to blast him with the waterproof spray.

383
00:21:03,288 --> 00:21:06,288
Tomorrow's when our badass revenge officially starts.

384
00:21:07,288 --> 00:21:08,288
We should probably get some rest.

385
00:21:09,288 --> 00:21:10,288
Yeah.

386
00:21:16,288 --> 00:21:17,288
Kay, done.

387
00:21:18,288 --> 00:21:20,288
This sure has been a hell of an article to write.

388
00:21:22,288 --> 00:21:24,288
Next month, they'll be doing a concert here.

389
00:21:26,288 --> 00:21:29,288
You can't dishonor the dead like that, I'll show him!

390
00:21:30,288 --> 00:21:31,288
What the hell?

391
00:21:32,288 --> 00:21:33,288
Are you kidding me?

392
00:21:34,288 --> 00:21:35,288
Mm-hmm.

393
00:21:36,288 --> 00:21:37,288
This is it.

394
00:21:38,288 --> 00:21:39,288
Get ready!

395
00:23:25,020 --> 00:23:32,020
Junko here. There's still a lot to be anxious about, but it would take a total catastrophe to stop us from at least giving it our best.

396
00:23:32,020 --> 00:23:38,020
Next time, Zombieland Saga Revenge Episode 11. All it takes is for you to be there, Saga. See you then!

